Filed from p5-mcp-wiki (binary-release spike, Getty/mcp-wiki-binary-spike, run 41587737077).

GitHub::CreateRelease creates the GitHub Release published and uploads the CPAN tarball afterwards; a failed upload is only logged. A workflow on `release: published` therefore starts before the tarball is there — the spike's binary workflow saw "no assets to download" 6 times before the asset appeared, and needs a retry loop (30 x 10 s).

Proposal: create the release as draft, upload the tarball, then publish (what `gh release create` does) — and make a failed upload fail the release step loudly. Relevant for the planned binary release form (`binary = ...` + shared `dzil-binary@v1` action), which downloads the tarball from the release.

